<body>

  <!-- Title & Academic Subtitle -->
  <h1>Buffon's Needle &amp; Noodle Problem: Monte Carlo &pi; Estimation</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Geometric Probability Parameter Mapping &amp; Central Limit Theorem Asymptotic Variance Analysis</div>

  <!-- Analytical Proof Header -->
  <div class="proof-box">
    <strong>Theoretical State Space &amp; Double Integral Derivation:</strong><br>
    Let parallel grid lines have spacing $D$, needle length $L \le D$. Let midpoint distance to the nearest line be $y \sim U(0, D/2)$ and orientation angle $\theta \sim U(0, \pi/2)$.<br>
    The uniform joint probability density over state space $\Omega = [0, D/2] \times [0, \pi/2]$ is $f(y, \theta) = \frac{1}{(D/2)(\pi/2)} = \frac{4}{\pi D}$.<br>
    The needle intersects a grid line if and only if $y \le \frac{L}{2}\sin\theta$.
    
    <div class="math-row">
      $$P = \iint_{\text{crossing}} f(y, \theta)\, dy\, d\theta = \frac{4}{\pi D} \int_{0}^{\pi/2} \left(\int_{0}^{\frac{L}{2}\sin\theta} dy\right) d\theta = \frac{4}{\pi D} \int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{L}{2}\sin\theta\, d\theta = \frac{2L}{\pi D}$$
    </div>

    <div class="math-row">
      $$\text{Estimator: } \hat{\pi} = \frac{2L}{\hat{P} \cdot D} = \frac{2 L N}{C D}, \qquad \text{Asymptotic Standard Error: } \text{SE}(\hat{\pi}) \approx \frac{\pi}{\sqrt{N}}\sqrt{\frac{\pi D}{2L} - 1} = O(1/\sqrt{N})$$
    </div>
  </div>

